90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (This report evaluates the security posture and architectural integrity of the Freelancer Escrow smart contract system. The protocol implements token-based escrow with third-party oracle voting for dispute resolution between businesses and freelancers. The most critical issue identified is improper enforcement of escrow lifecycle immutability. Escrow identifiers can be reinitialized, allowing state mutation and potential manipulation of majority thresholds. While arithmetic logic and reentrancy protections are largely correct, lifecycle boundaries are insufficiently enforced.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
