101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (The vote\(\) function validates voters against a global oracle registry but does not enforce membership within the escrow-specific oracle list. This weakens dispute isolation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Description: The createEscrow\(\) function does not enforce uniqueness of escrow identifiers. Any caller may recreate an existing escrow ID and overwrite its configuration, including oracle set, freelancer address, business address, and token address. Impact: Since vote counters are stored separately and majority is calculated dynamically from the oracle array length, an attacker may reduce quorum requirements and prematurely trigger release or refund logic. Root Cause: Escrow identity is treated as a reusable mapping key rather than an immutable lifecycle instance. Recommendation: Enforce escrow ID uniqueness prior to initialization and prevent state mutation after creation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
